WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.712
A RAG system must have a plan for document updates.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:09.277
Imagine that a policy changes but the old chunks remain in the vector database.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:16.172
Retrieval may continue returning outdated evidence even though the language model is working perfectly.

00:00:16.172 --> 00:00:24.452
A practical update workflow detects changed documents, removes or marks the old chunks, creates new chunks,

00:00:24.452 --> 00:00:28.320
generates new embeddings, and upserts the new records.

00:00:28.989 --> 00:00:32.371
Then the evaluation questions should be run again.

00:00:32.371 --> 00:00:37.806
Keep version information and updated dates in metadata whenever possible.

00:00:37.806 --> 00:00:47.611
Freshness is especially important for policies, product documentation, pricing, regulations, and internal procedures.

00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:52.051
Indexing is not a one-time activity in a living system.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:59.161
Production RAG needs a repeatable ingestion and re-indexing process so the knowledge base stays aligned with the

00:00:59.161 --> 00:01:01.574
underlying sources.
